// task.spawn accepts every Function and every BoundMethod, not only a
// user closure (spec/04-semantics.md, task.spawn step 1; issue #608). A
// native function (clock) and a bound native method (m.keys) are each a
// valid entry: the spawned task calls them with no arguments and discards
// the result. The closure entry sends to the main task, so the receive
// below proves all three spawns were accepted (a rejected one would end the
// program before the receive) and that the spawned tasks ran.
var main = task.self();

fun closureEntry() {
    print "closure-ran";
    task.send(main, "done");
}

var m = {"k": 1};

task.spawn(clock);                                                     // native Function
task.spawn(m.keys);                                                    // bound native method
task.spawn(closureEntry);                                              // user closure
print task.receive();

// STATUS: ok
// CHECK: closure-ran
// CHECK: done
